NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000031 "1;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000032 "# ABSTRACT: Simple minilanguage for use in expression"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000033 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000034 "__END__"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000035 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000036 "=pod"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000037 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000038 "=encoding UTF-8"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000039 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000040 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000041 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000042 "Language::Expr - Simple minilanguage for use in expression"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000043 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000044 "=head1 VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000045 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000046 "This document describes version 0.29 of Language::Expr (from Perl distribution Language-Expr), released on 2016-07-03."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000047 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000048 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000049 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000050 " use Language::Expr;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000051 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000052 " my $le = Language::Expr->new;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000053 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000054 " # convert Expr to string Perl code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000055 " say $le->get_compiler('perl')->compile('1 ^^ 2'); => # \"(1 xor 2)\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000056 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000057 " # convert Expr to JavaScript"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000058 " say $le->get_compiler('js')->compile('1 . 2'); # => \"'' + 1 + 2\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000059 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000060 " # evaluate Expr using the default interpreter"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000061 " say $le->get_interpreter('default')->eval('1 + 2'); # => 3"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000062 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000063 " # enumerate variables"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000064 " my $vars = $le->enum_vars('$a*$a + sqr($b)'); # => ['a', 'b']"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000065 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000066 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000067 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000068 "Language::Expr defines a simple, Perl-like expression minilanguage. It supports"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000069 "mathematical and string operators, arrays, hashes, variables, and functions. See"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000070 "L<Language::Expr::Manual::Syntax> for description of the language syntax."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000071 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000072 "This distribution consists of the language parser (L<Language::Expr::Parser>),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000073 "some interpreters (Language::Expr::Interpreter::*), and some compilers"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000074 "(Language::Expr::Compiler::*)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000075 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000076 "=head1 KNOWN BUGS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000077 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000078 "Due to possible bugs in Perl's RE engine or Regexp::Grammars or my"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000079 "grammar, some syntax errors will cause further parsing to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000080 "fail."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000081 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000082 "=head1 ATTRIBUTES"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000083 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000084 "=head1 METHODS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000085 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000086 "=head2 new()"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000087 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000088 "=head2 get_compiler($name) => obj"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000089 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000090 "Get compiler named C<$name>, e.g. C<perl>, C<js>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000091 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000092 "=head2 get_interpreter($name) => obj"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000093 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000094 "Get compiler named C<$name>, e.g. C<default>, C<var_enumer>, C<dummy>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000095 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000096 "=head1 FAQ"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000097 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000098 "=head2 Why yet another simplistic (restricted, etc) language? Why not just Perl?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000099 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000100 "When first adding expression support to L<Data::Schema> (now L<Data::Sah>), I"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000101 "want a language that is simple enough so I can easily convert it to Perl, PHP,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000102 "JavaScript, and others. I do not need a fully-fledged programming language. In"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000103 "fact, Expr is not even Turing-complete, it does not support assignment or loops."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000104 "Nor does it allow function definition (though it allows anonymous function in"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000105 "grep/map/usort). Instead, I just need some basic stuffs like"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000106 "mathematical/string/logical operators, arrays, hashes, functions,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000107 "map/grep/usort. This language will mostly be used inside templates and schemas."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000108 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000109 "=head2 Why don't you use Language::Farnsworth, or Math::Expression, or Math::Expression::Evaluator, or $FOO?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000110 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000111 "I need several compilers and interpreters (some even with different semantics),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000112 "so it's easier to start with a simple parser of my own. And of course there is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000113 "personal preference of language syntax."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000114 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000115 "=head2 What is the difference between a compiler and interpreter?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000116 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000117 "An interpreter evaluates expression as it is being parsed, while a compiler"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000118 "generates a complete Perl (or whatever) code first. Thus, if you $le->eval()"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000119 "repeatedly using the interpreter mode (setting $le->interpreted(1)), you will"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000120 "repeatedly parse the expression each time. This can be one or more orders of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000121 "magnitude slower compared to compiling into Perl once and then directly"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000122 "executing the Perl code repeatedly."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000123 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000124 "Note that if you use $le->eval() using the default compiler mode, you do not"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000125 "reap the benefits of compilation because the expression will be compiled each"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000126 "time you call $le->eval(). To save the compilation result, use $le->compile() or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000127 "$le->perl() and compile the Perl code yourself using Perl's eval()."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000128 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000129 "=head2 I want different syntax for (variables, foo operator, etc)!"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000130 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000131 "Create your own language :-) Fork this distribution and start"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000132 "modifying the Language::Expr::Parser module."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000133 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000134 "=head2 How to show details of errors in expression?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000135 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000136 "This is a TODO item."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000137 ""
